2. The document does not provide comparative data on update frequency between the official (Debian/RPM/Homebrew) packages and the community-maintained packages.
3. The document does not state whether the official packages undergo specific security audits beyond the general statements about maintainer support and deployment workflow.
4. The document does not define criteria used to classify an installation method as "Recommended (Official)" versus "Community (Unofficial)."
5. The document does not state whether packages listed as "Community (Unofficial)" are coordinated with the GitHub CLI maintainers in any way.
6. The document does not quantify the meaning of the warning against Snap beyond the statement that the team "actively discourages" snaps and references an external issue link.

